.TH SDL_ResetAssertionReport 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ResetAssertionReport \- Clear the list of all assertion failures.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_assert.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_ResetAssertionReport(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will clear the list of all assertions triggered up to that point\[char46] Immediately following this call,
.BR SDL_GetAssertionReport
will return no items\[char46] In addition, any previously-triggered assertions will be reset to a trigger_count of zero, and their always_ignore state will be false\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function is not thread safe\[char46] Other threads triggering an assertion, or simultaneously calling this function may cause memory leaks or crashes\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetAssertionReport (3)
